o a common denominator to compare them. The least common multiple of 7, 3, 8, and 8 is 168. Rewrite each fraction with the denominator 168:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{3 \\times 24}{7 \\times 24} = \\frac{72}{168}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{3} = \\frac{4 \\times 56}{3 \\times 56} = \\frac{224}{168}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} = \\frac{11 \\times 21}{8 \\times 21} = \\frac{231}{168}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{3 \\times 21}{8 \\times 21} = \\frac{63}{168}\n   \\]\n\n4. Compare the fractions with the common denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{63}{168}, \\frac{72}{168}, \\frac{224}{168}, \\frac{231}{168}\n   \\]\n\n5. The smallest fraction is \\(\\frac{63}{168} = \\frac{3}{8}\\) and the largest fraction is \\(\\frac{231}{168} = \\frac{11}{8}\\).\n\n6. Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least member:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\n   \\]\n\nThe positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set \\(\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}\\), we will first simplify and compare the fractions.\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{6}{16}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8}\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, we have the set \\(\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{3}{8}\\right\\}\\).\n\n3. Convert all fractions to a common denominator to compare them. The least common multiple of 7, 3, 8, and 8 is 168. Rewrite each fraction with the denominator 168:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{3 \\times 24}{7 \\times 24} = \\frac{72}{168}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{3} = \\frac{4 \\times 56}{3 \\times 56} = \\frac{224}{168}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} = \\frac{11 \\times 21}{8 \\times 21} = \\frac{231}{168}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{3 \\times 21}{8 \\times 21} = \\frac{63}{168}\n   \\]\n\n4. Compare the fractions with the common denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{63}{168}, \\frac{72}{168}, \\frac{224}{168}, \\frac{231}{168}\n   \\]\n\n5. The smallest fraction is \\(\\frac{63}{168} = \\frac{3}{8}\\) and the largest fraction is \\(\\frac{231}{168} = \\frac{11}{8}\\).\n\n6. Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least member:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\n   \\]\n\nThe positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).","id":"prealgebra:855"}
